  "description": "Piedmont's 1980s scheme: a white upper body over a polished bare-metal belly, the line between them straight just under the windows' level and curving down to the chin at the nose. A royal blue band through the cabin windows runs straight from the tail to the cockpit, where the whole nose ahead of the windshield is blue down to a line that slopes from the band's lower edge to the nose tip; white below it wraps the chin. 'PIEDMONT' in Piedmont's red slanted wordmark above the forward windows. A white fin with the blue speedbird (a flat bar pointed forward with three strokes rising back from it) over a smaller red 'PIEDMONT'. Polished engines. Worn by the 737-200s, 727-200s and the first 737-300s until the merger into USAir in August 1989.",
